.TH "GLESHA-MOVE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-move \- copy the history of a set to another remote
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha move\fR SET \-\-to REMOTE [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copy every snapshot and the catalog of SET to REMOTE, verify the copies, and make REMOTE the set's destination. Copies on the old remotes are kept. Sets with chunked snapshots cannot be moved.
.PP
Because \-\-to limits bucket access, name the current remotes with \-\-from. Objects in cold storage must be retrieved first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-assume\-yes
Answer yes to all confirmations.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
The new remote.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
The set's current remotes.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.SS Retrieval options
.TP
.B \-\-request\-retrieval
Allow charged cold retrieval without asking.
.TP
.B \-\-retrieval TIER
Tier: bulk, standard, or expedited (default: bulk). The default comes from the [cold] tier setting.
.TP
.B \-\-days N
Keep retrieved copies for N days (default: 3). The default comes from the [cold] days setting. A pending request keeps its original duration.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory, or 128MiB). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. On Linux, the default is half of the available memory. On other systems, or if the available memory cannot be read, the default is 128MiB.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Run up to N transfers at once (default: 4). The memory limit may lower the effective number.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Hash up to N files at once (default: 4).
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha move docs \-\-from aws \-\-to b2
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-configure (1),
.BR glesha\-storage\-class (1)
